{"repositoryId":1401969236,"availability":"available","full":"Gr33ndev/OpenAmpere","name":"OpenAmpere","description":"Local app for solar systems with battery storage, no cloud at all.","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T15:15:00Z","updated":"2026-10-12T19:00:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gr33ndev.github.io/OpenAmpere/","topics":["battery","evcc","foxess","hacs","hacs-integration","home-assistant","homeassistant-custom-component","modbus","solar"],"demo":"https://gr33ndev.github.io/OpenAmpere/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:35.553Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:35.553Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:35.553Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:35.553Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Local app for solar systems with battery storage, no cloud at all.","OpenAmpere talks to the inverter directly on your home network, stores all data locally and shows it in the browser. On a smartphone you can add the page to the home screen, and it then behaves like an app. No account, no cloud, no dependence on a manufacturer's server.","The app's user interface and the website are in German."],"features":["Menu: Übersicht (Overview), Geräte (Devices: operate the battery, wallbox and immersion heater, and set the order in which they get solar power), Auswertung (Report) and Mehr (More: setup and settings). A switch „Nur…","Live energy flow for PV, house, grid and battery with state of charge, plus wallbox and immersion heater","Solar by module array: power, voltage and current per PV input (MPPT), e.g. for the south roof, west roof or garage","Temperatures: inverter, battery, battery cells","Power curve over the day with state of charge, values on tap"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Gr33ndev/OpenAmpere/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"376a32996d69d924d7ec66ea075ba24312fb32051df1abce90